MCP stdio servers now start with the provider API keys unset by default. Committed as 19d5d3ce, titled "Part of #1064". It's local, so the push still happens at the end of the session. Build, the full cargo test run (34 test binaries), clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all pass.

The change: mcp_stdio_options() in src/mcp_prefix.rs now calls .env_remove_all(subprocess_env::hook_scrub_vars()). That is yoagent 0.26.8's new API, and it unsets the keys rather than setting them to "". It reuses the gate and key list hooks already have, so nothing new was written. Leaving YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB unset, or setting it to 1 or a misspelled value, scrubs the keys. Only 0 or false turns it off. GITHUB_TOKEN and GH_TOKEN are still passed through. Both places that start a server (the pre-flight tool listing and the real connect) go through this one function, and grep found no other site that starts a stdio server.

The cost to users: a server that quietly relied on inheriting your key will now fail its own calls. The fix is to give that one server the key in [mcp_servers.<name>] env = { KEY = "..." }. yoagent applies that map after the removal, so the key gets through, and a test confirms it. Setting YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0 also works. The model sees the same tool list as before.

Tests: I added tests/mcp_env_scrub.rs, six tests that run the real binary. The "server" is a small shell script that writes its environment to a file. The canary key is set only on the yoyo process the test starts, never in the test process itself.
• Unset, 1 and bogus: the key is absent.
• 0 and false: the key is passed through.
• An env map in the config: the explicit key arrives.
• Every case also checks that an ordinary variable arrived, so a server that never started can't make an "absent" test pass by accident.

Positive control: I replaced the removal list with an empty one (marked NEUTERED), ran the tests and restored the line in one command. Exactly the three scrub cases failed, by name, and the other three stayed green. After the restore all six pass and no marker is left.

Docs:
• safety.md has a new MCP row: the default, how to turn it off, the env-map fix and the cost.
• Two notes that still said MCP wasn't covered were wrong now, and I fixed both: the module doc in src/subprocess_env.rs (outside the task's file list, but only a comment) and the Day 238 "still open" line in ARCHITECTURE.md.
